# The file calls (roadmap l4.md L9), the OS server's, on the boot diskette
# (tests/programs/syscalls.asm's TEST_FILES checks): the current drive and
# A's directory; KERNEL.BIN found, and read back a sector at a time; a file
# refused as a directory; the root's one entry; the free bytes; drive B made
# current, and A again. Not on DOSBox-X: no interrupt from its diskette
# controller (docs/emulators.md).
program: syscalls
define: TEST_FILES
keys: x
timeout: 60
emulators: bochs mame
match: contains
---
files: drive 0 current
files: its directory \
files: \KERNEL.BIN, a file of {image_size} bytes
files: read back {image_size} bytes
files: a file's entries: error 18
files: a file as the directory: error 18
files: the root's entries 1
files: free {image_free} bytes
files: drive 1 current, then drive 0
